To support Python 3.15 lazy imports, modules whose names collide with objects exported
from their parent package have been moved to private modules. This affects
``qcodes.dataset.dond`` and its submodules, ``qcodes.utils.full_class``, the Stanford Research
driver modules (e.g. ``qcodes.instrument_drivers.stanford_research.SR830``) and the Basel
driver modules (e.g. ``qcodes.instrument_drivers.basel.BaselSP983``). The old module paths
remain available as deprecated aliases that emit a ``QCoDeSDeprecationWarning`` and will be
removed in a future release. Import the objects from the parent package instead, e.g.
``from qcodes.instrument_drivers.stanford_research import SR830`` or
``from qcodes.dataset import dond``.

Any other names that were importable from these modules but are not exported from the parent
package are now considered private. This includes the type aliases such as ``ParamMeasT`` and
``ActionsT``, as well as ``DondKWargs``, ``ParameterGroup``, ``ParameterSetEvent`` and
``catch_interrupts`` from ``qcodes.dataset.dond``. They remain importable from the deprecated
module aliases until those are removed. If you rely on one of these names, please open an issue
at https://github.com/microsoft/Qcodes/issues so that we can consider making it public.
